            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear Colleague, I am writing to inform you regarding your patient, an 84-year-old male admitted on 24/06/2007 with an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray revealed hyperinflation without consolidation. Blood tests and arterial blood gases confirmed respiratory insufficiency with hypoxaemia. Spirometry supported severe obstructive ventilatory impairment. During his brief inpatient stay, he was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy, resulting in satisfactory clinical improvement. Vital signs were monitored continuously. The patient was discharged in stable condition and is recommended for close follow-up, optimisation of inhaler technique, and pulmonary rehabilitation referral. Please do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
